#: ../../source/glob_README.md:34
msgid ""
"\"Globs\" are the patterns you type when you do stuff like `ls *.js` on "
"the command line, or put `build/*` in a `.gitignore` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Before parsing the path part patterns, braced sections are expanded into "
"a set.  Braced sections start with `{` and end with `}`, with any number "
"of comma-delimited sections within.  Braced sections may contain slash "
"characters, so `a{/b/c,bcd}` would expand into `a/b/c` and `abcd`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:42
msgid ""
"The following characters have special magic meaning when used in a path "
"portion:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:45
msgid "`*` Matches 0 or more characters in a single path portion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:46
msgid "`?` Matches 1 character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:47
msgid ""
"`[...]` Matches a range of characters, similar to a RegExp range. If the "
"first character of the range is `!` or `^` then it matches any character "
"not in the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:50
msgid ""
"`!(pattern|pattern|pattern)` Matches anything that does not match any of "
"the patterns provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:52
msgid ""
"`?(pattern|pattern|pattern)` Matches zero or one occurrence of the "
"patterns provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:54
msgid ""
"`+(pattern|pattern|pattern)` Matches one or more occurrences of the "
"patterns provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:56
msgid "`*(a|b|c)` Matches zero or more occurrences of the patterns provided"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:57
msgid "`@(pattern|pat*|pat?erN)` Matches exactly one of the patterns provided"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:59
msgid ""
"`**` If a \"globstar\" is alone in a path portion, then it matches zero "
"or more directories and subdirectories searching for matches. It does not"
" crawl symlinked directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:63
msgid "Dots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:65
msgid ""
"If a file or directory path portion has a `.` as the first character, "
"then it will not match any glob pattern unless that pattern's "
"corresponding path part also has a `.` as its first character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:69
msgid ""
"For example, the pattern `a/.*/c` would match the file at `a/.b/c`. "
"However the pattern `a/*/c` would not, because `*` does not start with a "
"dot character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:73
msgid ""
"You can make glob treat dots as normal characters by setting `dot:true` "
"in the options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:76
msgid "Basename Matching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:78
msgid ""
"If you set `matchBase:true` in the options, and the pattern has no "
"slashes in it, then it will seek for any file anywhere in the tree with a"
" matching basename.  For example, `*.js` would match "
"`test/simple/basic.js`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:83
msgid "Empty Sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:85
msgid ""
"If no matching files are found, then an empty array is returned.  This "
"differs from the shell, where the pattern itself is returned.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:92
msgid "To get the bash-style behavior, set the `nonull:true` in the options."
msgstr ""

