#: ../../source/glob_README.md:131
msgid "Class: glob.Glob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:133
msgid "Create a Glob object by instantiating the `glob.Glob` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:140
msgid ""
"It's an EventEmitter, and starts walking the filesystem to find matches "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:143
msgid "new glob.Glob(pattern, [options], [cb])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:145
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`pattern` `{String}` pattern to search for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:147
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`cb` `{Function}` Called when an error occurs, or matches are found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:151
msgid ""
"Note that if the `sync` flag is set in the options, then matches will be "
"immediately available on the `g.found` member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:154
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:156
msgid "`minimatch` The minimatch object that the glob uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:157
msgid "`options` The options object passed in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:158
msgid ""
"`aborted` Boolean which is set to true when calling `abort()`.  There is "
"no way at this time to continue a glob search after aborting, but you can"
" re-use the statCache to avoid having to duplicate syscalls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:161
msgid "`cache` Convenience object.  Each field has the following possible values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:163
msgid "`false` - Path does not exist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:164
msgid "`true` - Path exists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:165
msgid "`'FILE'` - Path exists, and is not a directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:166
msgid "`'DIR'` - Path exists, and is a directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:167
msgid ""
"`[file, entries, ...]` - Path exists, is a directory, and the array value"
" is the results of `fs.readdir`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:169
msgid ""
"`statCache` Cache of `fs.stat` results, to prevent statting the same path"
" multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:171
msgid ""
"`symlinks` A record of which paths are symbolic links, which is relevant "
"in resolving `**` patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:173
msgid ""
"`realpathCache` An optional object which is passed to `fs.realpath` to "
"minimize unnecessary syscalls.  It is stored on the instantiated Glob "
"object, and may be re-used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:177
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:179
msgid ""
"`end` When the matching is finished, this is emitted with all the matches"
" found.  If the `nonull` option is set, and no match was found, then the "
"`matches` list contains the original pattern.  The matches are sorted, "
"unless the `nosort` flag is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:183
msgid ""
"`match` Every time a match is found, this is emitted with the specific "
"thing that matched. It is not deduplicated or resolved to a realpath."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:185
msgid ""
"`error` Emitted when an unexpected error is encountered, or whenever any "
"fs error occurs if `options.strict` is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:187
msgid "`abort` When `abort()` is called, this event is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:189
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:191
msgid "`pause` Temporarily stop the search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:192
msgid "`resume` Resume the search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:193
msgid "`abort` Stop the search forever"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:195
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:197
msgid ""
"All the options that can be passed to Minimatch can also be passed to "
"Glob to change pattern matching behavior.  Also, some have been added, or"
" have glob-specific ramifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:201
msgid "All options are false by default, unless otherwise noted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:203
msgid "All options are added to the Glob object, as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:205
msgid ""
"If you are running many `glob` operations, you can pass a Glob object as "
"the `options` argument to a subsequent operation to shortcut some `stat` "
"and `readdir` calls.  At the very least, you may pass in shared "
"`symlinks`, `statCache`, `realpathCache`, and `cache` options, so that "
"parallel glob operations will be sped up by sharing information about the"
" filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:212
msgid ""
"`cwd` The current working directory in which to search.  Defaults to "
"`process.cwd()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:214
msgid ""
"`root` The place where patterns starting with `/` will be mounted onto.  "
"Defaults to `path.resolve(options.cwd, \"/\")` (`/` on Unix systems, and "
"`C:\\` or some such on Windows.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:217
msgid ""
"`dot` Include `.dot` files in normal matches and `globstar` matches. Note"
" that an explicit dot in a portion of the pattern will always match dot "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:220
msgid ""
"`nomount` By default, a pattern starting with a forward-slash will be "
"\"mounted\" onto the root setting, so that a valid filesystem path is "
"returned.  Set this flag to disable that behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:223
msgid ""
"`mark` Add a `/` character to directory matches.  Note that this requires"
" additional stat calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:225
msgid "`nosort` Don't sort the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:226
msgid ""
"`stat` Set to true to stat *all* results.  This reduces performance "
"somewhat, and is completely unnecessary, unless `readdir` is presumed to "
"be an untrustworthy indicator of file existence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:229
msgid ""
"`silent` When an unusual error is encountered when attempting to read a "
"directory, a warning will be printed to stderr.  Set the `silent` option "
"to true to suppress these warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:232
msgid ""
"`strict` When an unusual error is encountered when attempting to read a "
"directory, the process will just continue on in search of other matches."
"  Set the `strict` option to raise an error in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:236
msgid ""
"`cache` See `cache` property above.  Pass in a previously generated cache"
" object to save some fs calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:238
msgid ""
"`statCache` A cache of results of filesystem information, to prevent "
"unnecessary stat calls.  While it should not normally be necessary to set"
" this, you may pass the statCache from one glob() call to the options "
"object of another, if you know that the filesystem will not change "
"between calls.  (See \"Race Conditions\" below.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:243
msgid ""
"`symlinks` A cache of known symbolic links.  You may pass in a previously"
" generated `symlinks` object to save `lstat` calls when resolving `**` "
"matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:246
msgid "`sync` DEPRECATED: use `glob.sync(pattern, opts)` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:247
msgid ""
"`nounique` In some cases, brace-expanded patterns can result in the same "
"file showing up multiple times in the result set.  By default, this "
"implementation prevents duplicates in the result set.  Set this flag to "
"disable that behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:251
msgid ""
"`nonull` Set to never return an empty set, instead returning a set "
"containing the pattern itself.  This is the default in glob(3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:253
msgid "`debug` Set to enable debug logging in minimatch and glob."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:254
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`nobrace` Do not expand `{a,b}` and `{1..3}` brace sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:255
msgid ""
"`noglobstar` Do not match `**` against multiple filenames.  (Ie, treat it"
" as a normal `*` instead.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:257
msgid "`noext` Do not match `+(a|b)` \"extglob\" patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:258
msgid ""
"`nocase` Perform a case-insensitive match.  Note: on case-insensitive "
"filesystems, non-magic patterns will match by default, since `stat` and "
"`readdir` will not raise errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:261
msgid ""
"`matchBase` Perform a basename-only match if the pattern does not contain"
" any slash characters.  That is, `*.js` would be treated as equivalent to"
" `**/*.js`, matching all js files in all directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:264
msgid ""
"`nodir` Do not match directories, only files.  (Note: to match *only* "
"directories, simply put a `/` at the end of the pattern.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:266
msgid ""
"`ignore` Add a pattern or an array of glob patterns to exclude matches. "
"Note: `ignore` patterns are *always* in `dot:true` mode, regardless of "
"any other settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:269
msgid ""
"`follow` Follow symlinked directories when expanding `**` patterns. Note "
"that this can result in a lot of duplicate references in the presence of "
"cyclic links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:272
msgid ""
"`realpath` Set to true to call `fs.realpath` on all of the results. In "
"the case of a symlink that cannot be resolved, the full absolute path to "
"the matched entry is returned (though it will usually be a broken "
"symlink)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:276
msgid ""
"`absolute` Set to true to always receive absolute paths for matched "
"files.  Unlike `realpath`, this also affects the values returned in the "
"`match` event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:279
msgid ""
"`fs` File-system object with Node's `fs` API. By default, the built-in "
"`fs` module will be used. Set to a volume provided by a library like "
"`memfs` to avoid using the \"real\" file-system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:283
msgid "Comparisons to other fnmatch/glob implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:285
msgid ""
"While strict compliance with the existing standards is a worthwhile goal,"
" some discrepancies exist between node-glob and other implementations, "
"and are intentional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:289
msgid ""
"The double-star character `**` is supported by default, unless the "
"`noglobstar` flag is set.  This is supported in the manner of bsdglob and"
" bash 4.3, where `**` only has special significance if it is the only "
"thing in a path part.  That is, `a/**/b` will match `a/x/y/b`, but "
"`a/**b` will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:295
msgid ""
"Note that symlinked directories are not crawled as part of a `**`, though"
" their contents may match against subsequent portions of the pattern.  "
"This prevents infinite loops and duplicates and the like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:299
msgid ""
"If an escaped pattern has no matches, and the `nonull` flag is set, then "
"glob returns the pattern as-provided, rather than interpreting the "
"character escapes.  For example, `glob.match([], \"\\\\*a\\\\?\")` will "
"return `\"\\\\*a\\\\?\"` rather than `\"*a?\"`.  This is akin to setting "
"the `nullglob` option in bash, except that it does not resolve escaped "
"pattern characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:306
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If brace expansion is not disabled, then it is performed before any other"
" interpretation of the glob pattern.  Thus, a pattern like `+(a|{b),c)}`,"
" which would not be valid in bash or zsh, is expanded **first** into the "
"set of `+(a|b)` and `+(a|c)`, and those patterns are checked for "
"validity.  Since those two are valid, matching proceeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:312
msgid "Comments and Negation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:314
msgid ""
"Previously, this module let you mark a pattern as a \"comment\" if it "
"started with a `#` character, or a \"negated\" pattern if it started with"
" a `!` character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:318
msgid "These options were deprecated in version 5, and removed in version 6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:320
msgid "To specify things that should not match, use the `ignore` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:322
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:324
msgid "**Please only use forward-slashes in glob expressions.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:326
msgid ""
"Though windows uses either `/` or `\\` as its path separator, only `/` "
"characters are used by this glob implementation.  You must use forward-"
"slashes **only** in glob expressions.  Back-slashes will always be "
"interpreted as escape characters, not path separators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:331
msgid ""
"Results from absolute patterns such as `/foo/*` are mounted onto the root"
" setting using `path.join`.  On windows, this will by default result in "
"`/foo/*` matching `C:\\foo\\bar.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:335
msgid "Race Conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:337
msgid ""
"Glob searching, by its very nature, is susceptible to race conditions, "
"since it relies on directory walking and such."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:340
msgid ""
"As a result, it is possible that a file that exists when glob looks for "
"it may have been deleted or modified by the time it returns the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:343
msgid ""
"As part of its internal implementation, this program caches all stat and "
"readdir calls that it makes, in order to cut down on system overhead.  "
"However, this also makes it even more susceptible to races, especially if"
" the cache or statCache objects are reused between glob calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/glob_README.md:349
msgid ""
"Users are thus advised not to use a glob result as a guarantee of "
"filesystem state in the face of rapid changes.  For the vast majority of "
"operations, this is never a problem."
msgstr ""

